1
00:00:00,134 --> 00:00:07,644
A developer opens a file, changes it, and saves it. This is the first acceptance script for Open Editor.

2
00:00:08,256 --> 00:00:11,648
The page that hosts the workspace owns the files.

3
00:00:11,695 --> 00:00:18,116
It makes a store, with three calls: list, read and write. Here the store keeps its files in memory.

4
00:00:18,155 --> 00:00:21,397
Then one call builds the workspace on that store.

5
00:00:21,937 --> 00:00:27,399
Here is that page. Three files. Choose one, and it opens in a code editor.

6
00:00:27,449 --> 00:00:32,313
Type, and the line under the editor says the file has unsaved changes.

7
00:00:32,377 --> 00:00:37,177
Ctrl+F finds and replaces. Every amount becomes grams.

8
00:00:37,222 --> 00:00:42,129
Ctrl+S saves. The store receives the text, and the line says saved.

9
00:00:42,720 --> 00:00:50,464
A test plays these steps on every change, in three browsers. It reloads the page, and reads the saved text back.

10
00:00:50,383 --> 00:00:56,805
It also checks that a refused save says why, and that line endings come back as they went in.

11
00:00:57,388 --> 00:01:04,194
There is no new file, rename or delete yet. The author's script comes next. The guide has the rest.
